  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Oklahoma recorded $306M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. Oklahoma logged 593 awards with an average award size of $515K. Obligations fell 93.7% year over year. FY2027 obligations are smaller than recent fiscal years: FY26 obligations were $4.9B, FY25 obligations were $6.8B, FY24 obligations were $5.5B, FY23 obligations were $5B, and FY22 obligations were $5B. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer, obligating $242M. SIGNATURE CHOICE III, LLC is the largest vendor, receiving $226M. Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers is the largest industry category with $226M in obligations. Other notable buyers include the Department of Transportation with $24.5M and the Department of Justice with $21.5M. Other notable vendors include AAR AIRCRAFT SERVICES, INC. with $12.4M and several vendors in the top ten with obligations ranging up to $4.6M. All figures are contract obligations; FY2027 totals are partial fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
